Identify who Grand Duke Kirill Vladimirovich of Russia was and determine the identity of his wife, including her full name and background.
Grand Duke Kirill Vladimirovich of Russia was the second son of Emperor Alexander III of Russia and Empress Maria Feodorovna. He was born on 25 September 1873 and died on 24 May 1924. His wife was Grand Duchess Viktoria Feodorovna, also known as Princess Victoria Melita of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha. She was born on 10 June 1880 and was the daughter of Prince Albert Victor, Duke of Clarence and St Andrews, and his wife, Lady Alexandra Duff, Countess of Fife. She was a member of the British royal family and had German origins through her mother's side.
