Identify the full name and historical background of Prince Christopher of Greece and Denmark to determine his father's identity
Prince Christopher of Greece and Denmark, born Georgios Christoforos Konstantinos of Greece and Denmark, was the youngest child of King George I of Greece. He was born on 10 August 1888 in Pavlovsk, Imperial Russia, to King George I of Greece and his queen, Olga Constantinovna of Russia, a Russian grand duchess. His father, King George I of Greece, was a member of the House of Schleswig-Holstein-Sonderburg-Glücksburg and was the reigning monarch of Greece from 1913 until his death in 1913. Through his father, Prince Christopher was also a grandson of King Christian IX of Denmark, known as "the father-in-law of Europe" due to his numerous royal marriages.
